      {
        "question_text": "Fully simplify $\\frac{22}{55}$.",
        "solution_text": "The HCF of $22$ and $55$ is $11$.\n$\\frac{22}{55}=\\frac{22\\div11}{55\\div11}=\\frac{2}{5}$\n$2$ and $5$ share no common factor greater than $1$, so the fraction is fully simplified."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Fully simplify $\\frac{42}{70}$.\nStart by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2$.",
        "solution_text": "$\\frac{42}{70}=\\frac{42\\div2}{70\\div2}=\\frac{21}{35}$\n$21$ and $35$ still share the factor $7$.\n$\\frac{21}{35}=\\frac{21\\div7}{35\\div7}=\\frac{3}{5}$\n$3$ and $5$ share no common factor greater than $1$, so the fraction is fully simplified."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Fully simplify each fraction.\n(a) $\\frac{63}{27}$\n(b) $\\frac{13}{21}$\nExplain why the fraction in (b) does not change.",
        "solution_text": "(a) The HCF of $63$ and $27$ is $9$.\n$\\frac{63}{27}=\\frac{63\\div9}{27\\div9}=\\frac{7}{3}$\n$7$ and $3$ share no common factor greater than $1$.\n(b) Factors of $13$: $1$, $13$.\nFactors of $21$: $1$, $3$, $7$, $21$.\nThe only common factor is $1$, so $\\frac{13}{21}$ is already fully simplified."
      }
    ],
